<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esslingen am Neckar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esslingen am <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> is a city near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> that grew around a shrine of Saint Vitalis and a bridge over the Neckar. A free imperial city from the 13th century until 1802, it was a leading member of the Swabian city leagues, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-league">Swabian League</a> was founded there in 1488. It passed to Württemberg in 1802 and became an early centre of industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esslingen-am-neckar.jpg" alt="Esslingen am Neckar" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Qwerty123uiop · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Esslingen_a.N._Fall_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
